.SH "NAME"
roark\-metric\-variant\-list \- List a metric’s variants
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark metric variant list
\fIid\-or\-slug\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Every configuration of this metric your organization can use: Roark’s own variants and any your organization has added or forked. `isDefault` marks the one the metric is scored with when nothing pins another; pass any variant’s `id` as `sourceVariantId` to pin it on a derived metric. Auto\-managed variants (the ones a package materializes for you) are not listed: they are engine state, not configuration you author.
.SH "API"
GET /v1/metric/definitions/{idOrSlug}/variants
